diff --git a/docs/api_to_audit.md b/docs/api_to_audit.md
index ed330fc57d50a3041d2637e5d155038969cb3793..c92f29384e199312547cd2c95bc4ded01266edf5 100644
--- a/docs/api_to_audit.md
+++ b/docs/api_to_audit.md
@@ -3067,3 +3067,48 @@ Synchronous server-owned string middleware and completed render observations. Re
 Invalid middleware return types, exceptions, repeated continuation calls or missing/duplicate protected tokens fall back to the original default, with named logger diagnostics and an explicit observation fallback record. Observation middleware entries describe attempted execution, not successful overrides when fallback is present. Observers receive independent frozen samples with expanded visible default/final text; observer errors are logged. Promises are rejected as customization and rejection handlers prevent unhandled failures. Samples are render evidence, not proof of provider consumption. No core persistence or daemon protocol change is included.
 
 Stabilization requires auditing synchronous/reentrant behavior, stable prompt IDs and adapters across server, host/file, client/local and provider-owned content; verifying protected-resource reconstruction; documenting coverage/freshness and sample replay limits; and deciding observer privacy and retention policy. Prototype coverage is limited to implemented server adapters. SDK fake-host template rendering requires `experimental_p6rRenderPromptTemplate` injection and throws clearly when absent.
+
+## experimental_messageAdmission
+
+The optional backend member implements `NativeAdmissionProtocolV1` from the exact
+`@phosphorco/bb-message-admission/protocol` dependency. Native ingress and plugins
+share `getMessageAdmissionService(db)`; evaluation runs before native acceptance,
+while publication, evaluator generation and evidence are checked in the same
+transaction as the queue/request write. Immutable journal records reconcile
+stable operation IDs and retain per-thread acceptance activity after delivery or
+cancellation. Enrollment is explicit per project; installation and migration do
+not activate enforcement. Missing enrolled evaluators produce unresolved work.
+
+Stabilization requires the complete ingress census, real migrated database race
+and recovery witnesses, emitted SDK dependency conformance, and supported consumer
+adoption. Placement simulation uses the same native pure selector as queue insertion;
+request manifests read frozen journal mappings and activity uses the durable
+acceptance sequence. Feedback is advertised only while the native recovery
+coordinator has its normal submission ports configured. Full Send-now remains a
+disclosed override; live operational and execution checks remain mandatory.
+
+`MessageDispatchHookContext.experimental_admission` optionally carries the native
+phase (`prepared` or `accepted`) and every canonical `SubmissionV1` in dispatch
+order. Fresh submissions come from the prepared native ticket; accepted drains
+read the frozen native journal input. Plugins use this typed context for
+stateful dispatch guards without parsing text or legacy metadata. Core owns
+construction; this context grants no admission bypass. Stabilization includes
+all-original propagation and restart/retry witnesses in the native dispatcher.
+
+`ComposerSubmitOptions.operationId` optionally selects a nonblank native operation
+ID of at most 200 characters on either submission arm. The shared composer handle
+captures and validates it before awaiting uploads and forwards it to the host.
+The calling plugin still owns its opaque submission data through the native
+controller's plugin ID. A capable native host retains the chosen ID through the
+normal UI request path; exact retries reuse the same authored payload and key.
+Stabilization requires upload-wait retention, invalid-ID refusal, actual UI
+forwarding, and known/ambiguous native-operation reconciliation witnesses.
+
+A native feature guard's observed `message.dispatch` refusal may settle an
+unaccepted prepared operation as rejected. The result retains complete MR
+assessments and adds a separate `native-delivery-guard` assessment identifying
+the actual rejecting plugin, message and code, with contract revision
+`unversioned:message.dispatch`. The legacy runner stops at its first refusal;
+this record does not claim later legacy hooks ran. Missing plugin identity,
+exceptions and ambiguous failures remain unresolved. Accepted preparations
+retain their frozen admission.
